WasmFS: getcwd() drops the name of a mount point in a memory directory

Directory::Handle::getName() asks a directory that maintains file identity
for the name itself, and such a directory never knows the mount points in
its dcache, so getcwd() under a mount returned "/" or "//sub". Look in the
dcache first.

Upstream: https://github.com/emscripten-core/emscripten/issues/18112 (open; fix proposed in https://github.com/emscripten-core/emscripten/pull/23756)
Draft: docs/upstream/emscripten-wasmfs-getcwd-mount.md

diff --git a/system/lib/wasmfs/file.cpp b/system/lib/wasmfs/file.cpp
index c16af93..7fee432 100644
--- a/system/lib/wasmfs/file.cpp
+++ b/system/lib/wasmfs/file.cpp
@@ -207,15 +207,17 @@ int Directory::Handle::removeChild(const std::string& name) {
 }
 
 std::string Directory::Handle::getName(std::shared_ptr<File> file) {
-  if (getDir()->maintainsFileIdentity()) {
-    return getDir()->getName(file);
-  }
+  // Mount points are always in the dcache, even in directories that maintain
+  // file identity themselves, so look there first.
   auto& dcache = getDir()->dcache;
   for (auto it = dcache.begin(); it != dcache.end(); ++it) {
     if (it->second.file == file) {
       return it->first;
     }
   }
+  if (getDir()->maintainsFileIdentity()) {
+    return getDir()->getName(file);
+  }
   return "";
 }
 
